The problem here is you are only changing the `::backdrop`, which is a child of the `dialog`. When you close the `dialog`, it instantly goes away.
...
You only need to do the display and overlay transitions on the dialog itself, not the backdrop:
...
```css
dialog {
  opacity: 0;
  transition-property: opacity display overlay;
  transition-duration: 1s;
  transition-behavior: allow-discrete;
}
...
dialog[open] {
  opacity: 1;

  @starting-style {
    opacity: 0;
  }
}

dialog::backdrop {
  transition: opacity;
  transition-duration: 1s;
  backdrop-filter: blur(16px);
  background: hsl(0 0% 0% / 1);
  opacity: 0;
}

dialog[open]::backdrop {
  opacity: 1;
}

@starting-style {
  dialog[open]::backdrop {
    opacity: 0;
  }
}

```
